{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-48425",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[0,8],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(0)$ and $f(8).$\n\nSince $f(0)=0$ and $f(8)=2$, we must have \n$k\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is \"$0$ and $2$\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
